course: dictionary
lesson: 14474
title: The passer-by
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A passer-by is someone who walks past a place. The word comes from the verb pass, which means to go by. Passer is the person who passes, and passer-by is the form you will see most often in stories and news.
explain: «A passer-by heard the crash and ran to call for help.» The passer-by was not part of the crash. They were just walking past, and the word past is the clue. Ask yourself: who saw it, and what did they do?
explain: In sport, a passer is a player who passes the ball well. «Jess is a great passer, so her team always has the ball.» Here the words around passer, ball and team, tell you it is a player, not someone walking by.
fact: A passer-by is someone walking past a place, not someone who stops there to live or work.
fact: The plural of passer-by is passers-by: «Several passers-by stopped to look at the fire.»
fact: «Passer» means a person who passes, or a player who passes the ball to teammates.
fact: In sport, «a great passer» is a player who gives accurate passes that help the team score.
fact: Passer can also mean someone who passes a test or exam, but this meaning is rare.
exercise: «A passer-by saw the dropped wallet and picked it up.» Who is a passer-by? | A police officer on duty | *Someone walking past the place | A shop that sells wallets | The owner of the wallet
exercise: «Tom is a great passer, so his team scores lots of goals.» In this sentence, what is a passer? | A teacher who marks tests | *A player who passes the ball well | A person who sings loudly | A goalkeeper who never moves
exercise: «Many passers-by stopped to look at the fire.» What is the plural of passer-by? | passer-bys | passers-bys | *passers-by | passerbies
test: «The passers-by walked on without stopping.» Who are passers-by? | Children on the way to school | *People walking past | People who own the shop | Birds flying high above
test: «She is a passer who never misses her target.» In sport, what does passer mean here? | A painter of pictures | A swimmer who never stops | A writer of long stories | *A player who passes well
exam: Which description fits a passer-by best? | The owner of the shop | A player who scores every goal | A teacher marking a test | *Someone walking past who may stop to help
